{"name":"Country Linen","hex":"#d7c2a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"country","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The territory of a nation; a sovereign state or a region once independent and still distinct in institutions, language, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A large area regarded as distinct from other areas, e.g. because it is inhabited by a specific group of people"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["From or in the countryside, connected with it, or typical of it.","Of or connected to country music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/country"},{"term":"linen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Thread or cloth made from flax fiber.","Domestic textiles, such as tablecloths, bedding, towels, underclothes, etc., that are made of linen or linen-like fabrics of cotton or other fibers; linens."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from linen cloth or thread.","Having the colour linen, light beige."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Country","blocks":[{"text":"A country is a political entity or its territory in the world. They function as sovereign states, unrecognized states, constituent countries, or dependent territories. A country may consist of multiple nations, a structure known as a multinational state. Countries are often distinguished as developing countries or developed countries. There is no universal agreement on the number of \"countries\" in the world. This ambiguity is a result of several countries not being recognized as sovereign states by the UN system, but are recognized by at least one UN member, known as \"diplomatic recognition\". These countries often have disputed territories and have only partial recognition. A number of entities without recognition are also commonly considered a country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg/330px-Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country","wikidata":"Q6256"},{"title":"Linen","blocks":[{"text":"Linen is a textile made from the bast fibers of the flax plant. Linen cloth has been produced since ancient times primarily for use in clothing and household items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Handkerchief.jpg/330px-Handkerchief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linen","wikidata":"Q1426327"},{"title":"Shades of white","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of white are colors that differ slightly from the CIE standard illuminant D65, a white point that represents the average color of daylight at noon. There isn't one objectively pure white, as noon daylight varies by location and atmospheric conditions, and the choice of using D65 instead of direct sunlight or a white point on the Planckian locus is arbitrary. For simplicity, this article will use the term pure white for the D65 white point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Color_icon_white.svg/330px-Color_icon_white.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_white","wikidata":"Q7460350"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Oceania_without_Asian_country_codes.jpg/500px-Oceania_without_Asian_country_codes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Oceania_without_Asian_country_codes.jpg/500px-Oceania_without_Asian_country_codes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A number of non-sovereign entities nevertheless have country codes, such as PF (French Polynesia) and TK (Tokelau)","l